 knocked out the  electrical system to a level that  perhaps know when they anticipated now I  did not give that because the various  people I talked to said don't describe  the technique I just gave say there was  some technique here with no details no  description of the weapons delivery  system or even whether it was a weapon  no indication of how many targets would  be hit nothing just that it existed what  do you think of the one pardon what did  you think of the war still haven't fully  sorted out my own feelings on it is you  work on a book like this and get totally  immersed in it I have often found that  it's best to take my own sentiments and  conclusions and get them in my back  pocket and keep them there and I tend to  do that some of the reviewers of the  book of complained that I don't analyze  and take a stand or a position on things  and that's that just the way I do it I  feel more comfortable and quite frankly  i think that the sources from who may  have their own perspectives or an  analysis or policy goals see that i come  as a neutral and that I want to hear  what they have to say and that their  ideas and their analysis will be  presented in the book before I forget it  you were talking about sources earlier  and then again I've got to ask you the  obvious the deep throat question we use  some day reveal deep throat in history  yes when he is deceased when he is  decisions not when you're a deceased  when he's deceased who's going to go for  a lighted I alive well that's in again  no one planes for their own death and I  certainly fall in that category and I've  always said that I will reveal after he  is deceased how's this book doing  compared to all the other books you've  written well I've been fortunate that  all of the other books have been number  one bestsellers also so this is where  this book is is at the moment is it  selling more or less than those  bestsellers you get a sense of which  well the these books sell for a long  period of time many months and I don't  have numbers on it the people I've  talked to at Simon &amp; Schuster the  publisher and independent people say  it's out selling any book in the country  now quite a bit it is a recession  economy and books are expensive and the  people who are in the book business  would love to be selling more books but  when it's out selling any other book by  such a great deal you know I don't know  what measure you have beyond that All  the President's Men final days the  Brethren wired veil and now this book  which of all these books did you get the  biggest kick out it is it obvious that's  like no obvious in what sense obvious  that the the big seller All the  President's Men one that had the most  impact on or the final days I mean well  actually All the President's Men did not  outsell the others I think the one that  is sold the most so far is the one on  the Supreme Court the Brethren sold in  hardback about twice what All the  President's Men so I think each one of  these books it's like having at least so  far six children you  realize the strengths and weaknesses and  each of them you have an affection for  each of them they represent a certain  time in your life a certain commitment  certain effort to understand some part  of in the most of these cases government  and I I guess I tend to spend some time  reflecting on the deficiencies of all of  them and they they all have deficiencies  and trying to make each one better i  think some of the deficiencies have been  applied to the latter books but not  totally which one was the hardest hmm  good that's the hardest in the sense of  gathering the information you know  getting those sources to talk to you  I think the book unveil on the CIA  because the CIA is an institution that  plays a very ambiguous game with other  countries in the world within the  federal system in the national  government the people who were in the  CIA in a sense have been trained to  manipulate in DC so getting 