ad to  succeed we had to get Saddam Hussein's  forces out of Kuwait in ordered the war  if I'd published that say in december or  january i assume general Powell would  have gotten up and I  no they would have denied it but he  would have said whatever debate went  went on in October I now I'm totally  supporting the president's position and  I'm behind the effort that we were  making and the book demonstrates that  there was no one more active in making  sure that we had adequate force there  that we had the best equipment that they  were the best trained that all of the  details of the war plan were worked out  to succeed so I think in a way it would  have been a red herring and would have  had zero impact but then again you never  can tell without putting any names on  this as you were talking to your sources  both the high level and that's a high  level what did you sense the people  thought really thought of George Bush  during this whole process you mean  sources or principals involved in this  I'd say prints start with principles  well what the details I have of what  various individuals thought what Bush  said his key decision points are all  laid out in the book people have read it  reviewers people who bought the book and  called me received lots of letters and  so forth and some people have said it  makes bush look terrific decisive  forceful new the moral imperative he had  a grand strategic vision then there were  other people who've read it who said the  Bush White House is not well run he was  not sure that the procedures were very  random that the discussion among the key  Bush advisors was way too informal and  so forth so you know again you have the  best version I could get and it's laid  out and people have entirely different  reactions to it page 3 02 when the  principles matt bush like to keep  everyone around the  smiling jokes camaraderie the  conviviality of old friends positions  and alternatives were not completely  disgust interruptions w