itary man set  to the Pentagon kind of at the last  minute by Bush when the tower nomination  was defeated and janie learned the ropes  at the Pentagon learned the system got  into detail in a sense if you would look  for a model of civilian control of the  military he might represent it he  learned about war plans he learned about  weapon systems knows the White House  knows the Congress made sure that he was  not making the decision say about war  plans in the Gulf but spent the hours to  learn all the details and made sure that  they answered all of his questions  somebody who's feared somebody who's  respected somebody who isn't one of the  boys isn't you know inclined to go down  and have a beer on Friday afternoon with  the joint chiefs of staff or his own  staff somebody who's very business  oriented in the sense of the business of  the Pentagon somebody who if you look at  the constituencies  Secretary of Defense has to serve the  military the White House the Congress  the kind of world diplomatic scene he's  mastered them all here's a picture in  the book taken aboard military plane on  on its way to the Gulf that's right  that's the special VIP compartment in  the plane that their Cheney and Powell  are together do you get any sense after  your book came out that there have you  heard it all that their friction among  individuals who didn't realize they were  all talking to you oh I think they I  think they may have all learned  something I hope so and I think they I  have really not gone back I've talked to  a number of the people and had some  instant reactions none in depth yet  anybody call you and say Bob he did me  in no not at all you missed quoted me no  you misrepresented me I had a one army  person called me and say I got the  number of active divisions in the Army  wrong I think that's correct i did get  it wrong and unfortunately I relied on a  four-star general as my source and I  didn't check it what do you think of  what you learned about ge